# `.iago/` — {{PROJECT_NAME}} workspace (MWP L1)

**Client:** {{CLIENT_NAME}} · **Project:** {{PROJECT_NAME}} · **Created:** {{CREATED_DATE}}

**Layer:** L1 routing. Read after `CLAUDE.md` (L0), before anything under `.iago/`.
Budget ≤ 300 tokens — routing only, no content. The "where does X go" table lives
in `CLAUDE.md`; the `.iago/` schema itself is machine-enforced, not restated here.

## What is where

| Path | Layer | Holds |
|---|---|---|
| `PROJECT.md` | L3 | what and why, architecture, constraints |
| `ROADMAP.md` | L3 | the one roadmap — phase tables, not prose |
| `STATE.md` | L4 | the digest: ≤ 80 lines, `Updated:` mandatory |
| `_config/` | L3 | `runbooks/ context/ decisions/ learnings/ prompts/ hooks/` |
| `plans/` | L4 | `feature-{slug}/NN-{slug}.md`, `quick-{YYMMDD}-{slug}.md`, `_archive/` |
| `research/` | L4 | `YYYY-MM-DD-{slug}.md` |
| `summaries/` | L4 | `{plan-slug}.md`, written by the pipeline |
| `state/` | L4 | gitignored — locks, logs, per-run scratch |

Each directory carries a seed file explaining what belongs in it. Read that before
adding the first artefact of a new kind.

## Sub-workspaces

None yet. An inner app repo earns a row here — path, app repo, planning repo — the
day it is added. Its own nested `.iago/` may hold `state/` and nothing else; the
planning tree stays here, and the app repo gitignores `.iago/`.

## Conformance

From the iaGO-OS checkout: `python scripts/organize/iago-lint.py check --root
{{CLIENT_ID}}`. Non-zero exit is the worklist; each finding prints its own fix.
The schema, the banned list and the lifecycle table are in
`.iago/plans/feature-doc-standard/README.md` §2 and §6.
